WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.135
-Today is Friday,

00:00:02.135 --> 00:00:04.403
and that's usually when I catch
up on some personal stuff.

00:00:04.403 --> 00:00:06.873
You know, I check my inbox,
I return some e-mails,

00:00:06.873 --> 00:00:09.008
and of course,
I send out thank you notes.

00:00:09.008 --> 00:00:11.577
And I was running
a bit behind today,

00:00:11.577 --> 00:00:12.946
so I thought,
if you guys wouldn't mind,

00:00:12.946 --> 00:00:14.847
I'd just like to write out
my weekly thank you notes

00:00:14.847 --> 00:00:17.116
right now. Is that cool
with you guys?

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:18.985
Appreciate it.

00:00:19.352 --> 00:00:22.021
James, can I get some thank you
note-writing music, please?

00:00:22.021 --> 00:00:25.057
[ Solemn piano music plays ]

00:00:25.057 --> 00:00:26.525
Concentrating.

00:00:26.525 --> 00:00:27.626
[ Music stops ]

00:00:27.626 --> 00:00:30.162
-He looks like he's suspicious.

00:00:30.162 --> 00:00:31.064
-Shady.
-Worried about something.

00:00:31.064 --> 00:00:34.266
-Yeah, he did something,
you know.

00:00:34.266 --> 00:00:35.668
[ Music continues ]

00:00:35.668 --> 00:00:39.371
Thank you, Joe Biden,
for releasing your tax returns,

00:00:39.371 --> 00:00:41.073
although I'm not sure
you're actually allowed

00:00:41.073 --> 00:00:42.942
to deduct malarkey.

00:00:46.312 --> 00:00:47.847
[ Laughs ] What?

00:00:47.847 --> 00:00:49.314
Tried to deduct malarkey, huh?

00:00:49.314 --> 00:00:50.517
-And six pounds of it.

00:00:50.517 --> 00:00:51.784
-Oh, wow.

00:00:51.784 --> 00:00:53.252
♪♪

00:00:53.252 --> 00:00:56.289
Thank you, Kim Jong-un,
banning mullets

00:00:56.289 --> 00:00:58.591
and skinny jeans,

00:00:58.591 --> 00:01:00.392
for letting the world know
that your biggest enemy

00:01:00.392 --> 00:01:03.462
is apparently Billy Ray Cyrus
from 1992.

00:01:03.462 --> 00:01:04.931
What's your problem?

00:01:08.234 --> 00:01:11.304
Achy-breaky. [ Sniffs ]

00:01:11.304 --> 00:01:14.407
Thank you,
getting handed your diploma,

00:01:14.407 --> 00:01:16.075
for making me feel like
I'm participating

00:01:16.075 --> 00:01:18.778
in a relay race
that took four years to finish.

00:01:24.884 --> 00:01:25.985
[ Laughs ]

00:01:27.353 --> 00:01:28.721
♪♪

00:01:28.721 --> 00:01:31.157
Thank you,
graduation ceremonies,

00:01:31.157 --> 00:01:33.426
for giving
students one final lesson --

00:01:33.426 --> 00:01:36.695
how to dodge sharp pieces
of falling cardboard.

00:01:37.329 --> 00:01:38.765
[ Imitates whooshing ]

00:01:39.765 --> 00:01:41.867
[ Trills tongue ]

00:01:42.668 --> 00:01:46.605
Hoo! Hoo! Psh!
[ Trills tongue ]

00:01:46.605 --> 00:01:49.074
They have any Avengers that
throw things like that?

00:01:49.074 --> 00:01:52.044
-Don't they have, like,
that card guy, like, Gambit

00:01:52.044 --> 00:01:53.179
or something like that?

00:01:53.179 --> 00:01:54.513
-Oh, really?
-Yeah.

00:01:54.513 --> 00:01:55.982
-The gambler, he comes out
and he just takes the card

00:01:55.982 --> 00:01:58.484
out of the deck of cards
and flips it at somebody?

00:01:58.484 --> 00:02:00.986
That's it's pretty cool.
Does he trick first

00:02:00.986 --> 00:02:02.255
and have them guess it?
-Maybe that's like --

00:02:02.255 --> 00:02:04.556
-Your own murder weapon.
He's like, "Yeah but then --

00:02:04.556 --> 00:02:07.360
but then Susie and Timmy,
they went to the store,

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:09.028
so then they got rid of it."

00:02:09.028 --> 00:02:10.462
You know, they do
the whole story.

00:02:10.462 --> 00:02:14.066
And they're like, "Well then,
well, where's Timmy?"

00:02:14.066 --> 00:02:16.402
"This it?" And, you go,
"No, it's actually not."

00:02:16.402 --> 00:02:18.137
He's like, "Well, I guess I
don't know how

00:02:18.137 --> 00:02:19.772
to do magic, then."

00:02:23.542 --> 00:02:24.877
"Wait a second.

00:02:24.877 --> 00:02:26.980
Can you just check
your coat pocket for a second?"

00:02:33.553 --> 00:02:35.221
It's Timmy!

00:02:35.221 --> 00:02:37.456
And then you give it to him,
and he takes it and he goes,

00:02:37.523 --> 00:02:38.324
[ Trilling tongue ]

00:02:38.324 --> 00:02:40.159
Oooh!

00:02:40.159 --> 00:02:41.360
-Is this your card?

00:02:41.360 --> 00:02:43.496
-Yeah. [ Laughs ]

00:02:43.496 --> 00:02:45.165
-You cut off my finger.
-[ Laughs ]

00:02:47.800 --> 00:02:49.501
♪♪

00:02:49.501 --> 00:02:53.006
Thank you, churros,
for being the only dessert

00:02:53.006 --> 00:02:55.942
that looks like it was made
using a Play-Doh Fun Factory.

00:02:58.744 --> 00:03:00.380
-That's not a churro.

00:03:05.585 --> 00:03:06.919
♪♪

00:03:06.919 --> 00:03:09.488
Thank you, Las Vegas
Hustler Club's

00:03:09.488 --> 00:03:12.692
pop-up vaccine site

00:03:12.692 --> 00:03:16.195
for not being the first pop-up
that's happened at a strip club.

00:03:16.195 --> 00:03:17.563
-Oh, hey!

00:03:17.563 --> 00:03:18.598
[ Rim shot ]

00:03:18.598 --> 00:03:20.766
Uh-oh!

00:03:20.766 --> 00:03:22.535
Oy!

00:03:22.535 --> 00:03:24.804
Polling station?
-No.

00:03:27.306 --> 00:03:32.177
[ Laughs ] Johnson &amp;...Johnson.
-[ Laughs ] Hey!

00:03:32.177 --> 00:03:34.947
-Three -- three Johnsons.

00:03:34.947 --> 00:03:36.515
-[ Blowing ] Get ready for it.

00:03:36.515 --> 00:03:37.917
You can do it,
you can do it.

00:03:37.917 --> 00:03:39.251
You got them ready?

00:03:39.251 --> 00:03:42.154
-Do I got what ready?

00:03:42.154 --> 00:03:43.790
-Is that your card?

00:03:46.692 --> 00:03:50.762
That wasn't my card.
[ Groans ]

00:03:51.029 --> 00:03:51.964
[ Rim shot ]

00:03:51.964 --> 00:03:54.500
-That's right. This was.

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:56.468
-[ Shouting ] You're right.

00:03:56.468 --> 00:04:00.873
It was the Seven of Spades.
[ Groaning ]

00:04:02.075 --> 00:04:03.876
Wait, this card is a Joker.

00:04:03.876 --> 00:04:07.446
So, yes, it was my card.
I'm dying now.

00:04:07.446 --> 00:04:09.749
I'm about to lose my life.
Let me --

00:04:09.749 --> 00:04:12.885
-Hey, hey.
-I know --

00:04:12.885 --> 00:04:15.922
-[ Groans, trills tongue ]

00:04:15.922 --> 00:04:20.660
This is a card for 20% off
at Bed Bath &amp; Beyond.

00:04:20.660 --> 00:04:22.395
Ah! I think I'm beyond that!

00:04:22.395 --> 00:04:24.363
-[ Laughs ] Here you go, then.

00:04:24.363 --> 00:04:27.900
-[ Shouting ] Oh, my gosh.
This is a Diner's Club card

00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:29.768
for 60s free --

00:04:29.768 --> 00:04:30.770
-Let's just call it
a misunderstanding.

00:04:30.770 --> 00:04:31.604
I'll see you next week, OK?

00:04:31.604 --> 00:04:32.771
-OK, alright.

00:04:32.771 --> 00:04:33.973
[ Imitates popping ] Oh.

00:04:33.973 --> 00:04:35.174
-Here we go.

00:04:35.174 --> 00:04:36.375
♪♪

00:04:36.375 --> 00:04:39.312
Thank you, cabinet full of
old spices.

00:04:39.312 --> 00:04:41.213
It's nice to know
I can freshen up any meal

00:04:41.213 --> 00:04:44.583
with some garlic powder
from 2006.

00:04:44.583 --> 00:04:45.752
C'mon, it still works.

00:04:45.752 --> 00:04:47.886
Just bang it on the counter.

00:04:47.886 --> 00:04:50.289
-It's solid now.
-Exactly.

00:04:50.289 --> 00:04:52.057
You scrape it off, like...
[ imitates scraping ]

00:04:52.057 --> 00:04:53.826
-You just get a grater.
-Yeah.

00:04:53.826 --> 00:04:57.163
-Makes it better,
because it's "grater."

00:04:58.698 --> 00:05:00.766
-A little cheesy...
-Nice.

00:05:00.766 --> 00:05:02.969
-...But still sharp.
-Ah!

00:05:04.603 --> 00:05:06.272
That was a "gouda" joke.

00:05:08.274 --> 00:05:10.276
[ Rim shot ]

00:05:10.276 --> 00:05:13.246
-Yeah, I guess we're
"fonduing" it.

00:05:13.579 --> 00:05:15.548
[ Rim shot ]

00:05:16.615 --> 00:05:17.884
♪♪

00:05:17.884 --> 00:05:20.953
Thank you, crayons,
for starting out pristine

00:05:20.953 --> 00:05:22.655
and ending up like
a post-battle scene

00:05:22.655 --> 00:05:23.923
from "Game of Thrones".

00:05:23.923 --> 00:05:25.725
There you have it.
Those are our thank you notes.

